{"id": "striviaqa0053", "pool": "striviaqa", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2712938540, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "36fb1f5a6d3150bc9e2924638613014e95b57ee10045021a2cba34cf44c19605", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "Which Kent brewer is believed to be the oldest continuous brewer in the country?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/striviaqa0053.wav", "input_sha256": "6fc2b919a86ee03aa47b09b744a1fbee538a7dec197fbea534b3f6dae6dc7556", "input_samples": 74766, "input_s": 4.673, "n_real_chunks": 5, "score": 0.8802, "act": 0.9999, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "False. Shepherd Neame is generally described as Britain’s oldest brewer, tracing its history to 1698. Wychwood Brewery was founded much later and its Witney brewery closed in November 2023. (shepherdneame.co.uk)", "expert_answer": "False. **Shepherd Neame** is generally described as **Britain’s oldest brewer**, tracing its history to **1698**. Wychwood Brewery was founded much later and its Witney brewery closed in **November 2023**. ([shepherdneame.co.uk](https://www.shepherdneame.co.uk/about-us?utm_source=openai))", "transcript": "Wychwood Brewery is believed to be the oldest continuous brewer in the country.\n", "asr_s": 0.84, "expert_s": 5.17, "expert_input_samples": 74766, "expert_input_s": 4.673, "expert_input_sha256": "6fc2b919a86ee03aa47b09b744a1fbee538a7dec197fbea534b3f6dae6dc7556", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 5.709, "relay_synth_ms": 6711, "onset_chunk": 5, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/striviaqa/audio/striviaqa0053_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "452443db1468e99fffb90bc847a07288e5ca9ebee2417acd70a5c7d1